From 48bea6130a4be3cb5bdfc4a0a373b0fd0dd74286 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TrinityXSX <trinityxsx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:57:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add network keyboard and mouse input (TXIN over UDP)

A PC's keyboard and mouse reach Wine over the LAN: TrinityXSX's
tools/netinput-sender captures them on Windows (Ctrl+Alt+F12) and sends
one 64-byte UDP datagram per change, plus a heartbeat, to port 9396.

src/pw_netinput.c decodes TXIN v1. Each datagram carries the whole state
(held virtual keys, buttons, and motion and wheel as running totals), so
a lost datagram is mended by the next one. The receiver follows one
sender at a time, from a private address only, and releases everything
it held after 500 ms of silence. Left and right Shift, Ctrl and Alt become
the generic keys, as the USB keyboard's do.

native/pw_netinput_ps5.c reads a non-blocking libSceNet socket once a
tick; the title loop posts the result through pw_wine_post_input next to
the USB keyboard and mouse, with the same rule while the console's
keyboard is up.
